              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Federal Maritime Commission argues that adjudicating a Shipping Act complaint is an administrative regulatory process that involves making findings of fact and applying its interpretation of the Shipping Act, constituting an exercise of executive power."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "58aecba757f09cdf0ae3ee54ad64b8050c4c79a2820a2e70a6d427e0a1601f3d",
