          "text": "According to Federal Maritime Commission, the adjudication of a Shipping Act complaint by the Federal Maritime Commission is an administrative regulatory process through which the agency makes findings of fact and applies its interpretation of the Shipping Act to those findings of fact. This is an exercise of executive power."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Federal Maritime Commission",
